# Event record schema

Every event a detector produces is an `Event` with: `city`; `event_type` (one of
`temp_anomaly`, `precipitation`, `frontal_passage`, `apparent_gap`); `started_at`;
`ended_at` (`None` while ongoing); `severity` (`None` where the detector does not
grade severity); a plain-language `reason` string explaining WHY it fired; and an
optional `detail` dict of supporting numbers. Dedup identity is
`(city, event_type, started_at)`. Persist via `upsert_event`
(`INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE`), which fills `ended_at` when an open event
later closes — never insert a duplicate. `detail` is JSON-encoded on write,
decoded on read.

**Rationale:** the `reason` string and dedup identity are what make events
self-explanatory and idempotent across recompute cycles — required because
detection re-runs over history every poll.
